From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:39:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Skip a reserved area that the aligned start passes in
 map_reserved_area().

Rounding an area's start up to the alignment can pass the area's end;
the negative difference, compared with the unsigned size, passed the
size check, and the view was placed past the area, over an allocated
one (create_view's VPROT_SYSTEM assertion). snmalloc's size-aligned
VirtualAlloc2 reservations, which mtld3d makes, reach it in the macOS
soft pagezero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index cca9479..2f96a37 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -1840,7 +1840,7 @@ static void *map_reserved_area( void *limit_low, void *limit_high, size_t size,
         {
             if (mem_area_state( area ) != AREA_RESERVED) continue;
             start = ROUND_ADDR( (char *)mem_area_base( area ) + align_mask, align_mask );
-            if ((char *)end - (char *)start < size) continue;
+            if (start >= end || (char *)end - (char *)start < size) continue;
             ptr = ROUND_ADDR( (char *)end - size, align_mask );
             break;
         }
@@ -1853,7 +1853,7 @@ static void *map_reserved_area( void *limit_low, void *limit_high, size_t size,
             if (mem_area_state( area ) != AREA_RESERVED) continue;
             start = ROUND_ADDR( (char *)start + align_mask, align_mask );
             end = min( limit_high, mem_area_end( area ));
-            if ((char *)end - (char *)start < size) continue;
+            if (start >= end || (char *)end - (char *)start < size) continue;
             ptr = start;
             break;
         }
